          ],
          "content": "7. Complete the following flow chart:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.106,
            0.853,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.345,
            0.883,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "8. You are provided with the following materials. Discuss which material would be your choice to make a pan that is most suitable for boiling water and why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.265,
            0.414,
            0.873,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": "Iron copper sulfur coal plastic wood cardboard"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.446,
            0.882,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "9. You are provided with three iron nails, each dipped in oil, water and vinegar. Which iron nail will not rust, and why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.487,
            0.883,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": "10. How do the different properties of metals and non-metals determine their uses in everyday life?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.527,
            0.883,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": "11. One of the methods of protecting iron from getting rusted is to put a thin coating of zinc metal over it. Since sulfur does not react with water, can it be used for this purpose? Justify your answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.605,
            0.883,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": "12. An ironsmith heats iron before making tools. Why is heating necessary in this process?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.657,
            0.545,
            0.68
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Exploratory Projects"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.701,
            0.884,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": "Dhokra, Bidriware, Pembarthi, and Kamrupi are some of India’s famous metal art styles. Find out the states where these artworks are made. Also, make a collage of their photographs."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.779,
            0.882,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": "On a map of India, mark the states where iron, gold, aluminium and other metals are found."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.82,
            0.883,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": "Explore the metals and non-metals found in smartphones and find out how they help the phone work properly."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.86,
            0.883,
            0.9
          ],
          "content": "Organise a classroom debate on whether the use of metals for comfort and luxury should be increased or decreased."
        },
